vLLM (model plugin code)
  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
  Copyright contributors to the vLLM project.
  - rcp-ndcg-vllm/src/rcp_ndcg_vllm/models/topk/model.py: `TopkEmbedModel` subclasses
    `vllm.model_executor.models.colqwen3_5.ColQwen3_5Model` (vLLM v0.31.0) and
    reuses its weight mapping, pooling wiring and forward pass unmodified.
  - rcp-ndcg-vllm/src/rcp_ndcg_vllm/models/topk/weights.py: the checkpoint-name mapping table
    restates the prefix mappings of `vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_vl.py`
    (`hf_to_vllm_mapper`) so the tests can verify the served mapping without
    importing vLLM.
  - rcp-ndcg-vllm/src/rcp_ndcg_vllm/models/pplx/: the PplxContextualModel is a thin
    subclass of vLLM's own `Qwen3_5ForCausalLMBase` (Apache-2.0, vLLM project); the
    subclasses where that inheritance ends at it, and every line that adapts the
    checkpoint's naming or pooling, is this repository's own.

The topk model class is written for the checkpoint of
topk-io/topk-embed-v1-small (Apache-2.0) at revision
e54485ebab921f2c18c4d092b3f4c40dcca26781; the pplx model class for
perplexity-ai/pplx-embed-v2-context-9b-preview (MIT, by its authors). Neither
plugin vendors weights and neither performs downloads.

